  "result": "I added reservations with expiry to the store and the API, plus new tests. `npm test` passes with 176 tests, none failing.\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable` follow your spec.\n- Time comes only from the store's `clock` option.\n- `removeItem` now throws `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` if the quantity is more than what's available, so it can't take reserved stock.\n- `getStock` still returns physical stock.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` also returns `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you specified.\n\n**Choices the spec left open**\n- `confirm` also returns `{sku, stock}` from the store, which is what the confirm route uses for its response.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 400 for any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK`.\n- I didn't validate `ttlMs`.\n- Expired reservations stay in memory and are never cleaned up. They stop counting against availability, and `confirm` on them keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n\n**Tests**\n- New store tests are in `test/store.test.js`, covering reserve, expiry at exactly creation + ttl, confirm, release and `removeItem` with reservations.\n- New API tests are in `test/api.test.js`.\n\nI haven't made any git commits.",
